    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0427" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Executive Secretariat Files: NSC 37/10</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the National Security
                            Council
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        NSC 37/10</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-08-03">August 3, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Immediate United States Courses of Action With
                        Respect to Formosa</hi>
                </p>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#top">References:</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">A. NSC
                            Action No. 325 [<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>]<anchor n="1"
                                xml:id="d240-f1"/></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">B. Memo for NSC from Executive Secretary, subject: “General Policy of
                            the United States Concerning Formosa”, dated July 28, 1950<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d240-f2"/></cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>The enclosed statement of policy on the subject, approved by the Secretaries of
                    State and Defense in accordance with the President’s approval in principle of
                    the recommendations contained in the reference memorandum (NSC Action No. 325–<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>),
                    is circulated herewith for the information of the National Security Council and
                    the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>As requested by representatives of the Secretaries of State and Defense, <pb
                        facs="0428" n="414" xml:id="pg414"/> the memorandum by the Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff on “General Policy of the United States Concerning Formosa”, attached to
                    the reference memorandum, is included herewith as an Appendix.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d240-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay,
                            Jr</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d240-a1.xml" xpointer="d240-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d240-f1" n="1" xml:id="d240-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 6 to the memorandum by the Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Secretary of
                    Defense, July 27, <ref target="#pg394">p. 394</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d240-f2" n="2" xml:id="d240-f2-content">
                <p>Mr. Lay’s memorandum of July 28, not printed, merely forwarded the JCS memorandum to the Secretaries of State and
                    Defense with the request that their final agreed statement on policy be
                    transmitted to the National Security Council.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d240-f3" n="3" xml:id="d240-f3-content">
                <p>The JCS memorandum is printed under date of July
                    27, <ref target="#pg391">p. 391</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
